  -
    title: "Why Self-Attention"
    start_index: 6
    end_index: 5
    nodes:
      [1,]{title,start_index,end_index,summary,split_document_anchor,chunk_excerpt_index,node_id}:
        Computational Complexity and Parallelization,5,7,The section discusses the computational complexity and parallelization capabilities of self-attention layers compared to recurrent and convolutional layers.,In this section we compare various aspects of self-attention layers to the recurrent and convolu- tional layers commonly used for mapping one variable-length sequence of symbol representations,0,0016
    summary: "This section compares self-attention layers to recurrent and convolutional layers, highlighting the advantages of self-attention in terms of computational complexity and parallelization."
    split_document_anchor: "4 Why Self-Attention"
    chunk_excerpt_index: 0
